gfs2: Get rid of GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS

jira KERNEL-1773
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10
commit-author Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
commit bddb53b776fb7ce81dfba7c24884d9f2c0c68e50
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10/bddb53b7.failed

Get rid of the GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS flag: it was originally used
to indicate to add_to_queue() that the ->go_sync() and ->go_invalid()
operations were in progress, but as we have established in commit "gfs2:
Fix LM_FLAG_TRY* logic in add_to_queue", add_to_queue() has no need to
know.

Commit d99724c3c36a describes a race in which GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS
is used to serialize two processes which are both in do_xmote() at the
same time.  That analysis is wrong: the serialization happens via the
GLF_LOCK flag, which ensures that at most one glock operation can be
active at any time.

Fixes: d99724c3c36a ("gfs2: Close timing window with GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS")
	Signed-off-by: Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
	Reviewed-by: Andrew Price <anprice@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit bddb53b776fb7ce81dfba7c24884d9f2c0c68e50)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/gfs2/glock.c
#	fs/gfs2/trace_gfs2.h
diff --cc fs/gfs2/glock.c
index 3a2c524fb00c,e8b630a58da8..000000000000
--- a/fs/gfs2/glock.c
+++ b/fs/gfs2/glock.c
@@@ -2343,10 -2304,8 +2331,15 @@@ static const char *gflags2str(char *buf
  		*p++ = 'y';
  	if (test_bit(GLF_LFLUSH, gflags))
  		*p++ = 'f';
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	if (test_bit(GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS, gflags))
 +		*p++ = 'i';
 +	if (test_bit(GLF_MAY_CANCEL, gflags))
 +		*p++ = 'c';
++=======
+ 	if (test_bit(GLF_PENDING_REPLY, gflags))
+ 		*p++ = 'R';
++>>>>>>> bddb53b776fb (gfs2: Get rid of GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS)
  	if (test_bit(GLF_HAVE_REPLY, gflags))
  		*p++ = 'r';
  	if (test_bit(GLF_INITIAL, gflags))
diff --cc fs/gfs2/trace_gfs2.h
index 0f6e4e931211,1c2507a27318..000000000000
--- a/fs/gfs2/trace_gfs2.h
+++ b/fs/gfs2/trace_gfs2.h
@@@ -52,8 -52,7 +52,12 @@@
  	{(1UL << GLF_DEMOTE_IN_PROGRESS),	"p" },		\
  	{(1UL << GLF_DIRTY),			"y" },		\
  	{(1UL << GLF_LFLUSH),			"f" },		\
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	{(1UL << GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS),	"i" },		\
 +	{(1UL << GLF_MAY_CANCEL),		"c" },		\
++=======
+ 	{(1UL << GLF_PENDING_REPLY),		"R" },		\
++>>>>>>> bddb53b776fb (gfs2: Get rid of GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS)
  	{(1UL << GLF_HAVE_REPLY),		"r" },		\
  	{(1UL << GLF_INITIAL),			"a" },		\
  	{(1UL << GLF_HAVE_FROZEN_REPLY),	"F" },		\
* Unmerged path fs/gfs2/glock.c
diff --git a/fs/gfs2/incore.h b/fs/gfs2/incore.h
index 445946dcd461..603a308c5786 100644
--- a/fs/gfs2/incore.h
+++ b/fs/gfs2/incore.h
@@ -322,7 +322,6 @@ enum {
 	GLF_DEMOTE_IN_PROGRESS		= 5,
 	GLF_DIRTY			= 6,
 	GLF_LFLUSH			= 7,
-	GLF_INVALIDATE_IN_PROGRESS	= 8,
 	GLF_HAVE_REPLY			= 9,
 	GLF_INITIAL			= 10,
 	GLF_HAVE_FROZEN_REPLY		= 11,
